    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ce66d273-2ed5-5c4d-9a01-fc8eed71d4ba",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 9 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -7 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{2}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{3}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the third and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 9 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -7 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{3}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{2} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 9 & 4 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
