      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -9 & -9 \\\\ -3 & -9 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -7 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{2}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the second and third rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -9 & -9 \\\\ -3 & -9 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -7 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{2}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -9 & -9 \\\\ -8 & -7 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -9 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
